  {
    "id": "45f73fa0-6a6d-5786-8d87-b07f026e83ca",
    "pack": "secrets-of-magic",
    "kind": "class-feature",
    "slug": "class-feature:flexible-spell-preparation",
    "name": "Flexible Spell Preparation",
    "level": 1,
    "rarity": "common",
    "traits": [],
    "sources": [
      {
        "kind": "book",
        "book": "secrets-of-magic"
      }
    ],
    "description": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "This class feature alters your spellcasting class feature (such as Arcane Spellcasting for the wizard or Divine Spellcasting for the cleric). If you choose this class archetype, you must select "
          },
          {
            "type": "ref",
            "id": "9afc6433-5bf8-5462-8c06-82f5449ef03c"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " as your 2nd-level class feat."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "ordered": false,
        "items": [
          [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "You can cast fewer spells each day. Your number of spell slots per day don't advance from 2 to 3 spells at even levels."
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "Reduce the number of cantrips you gain from your class by 2. This archetype doesn't change the way you prepare cantrips."
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "During your daily preparations, you prepare a spell collection rather than preparing spells into each spell slot individually. The number of spells in your spell collection each day equals the total number of spell slots you get each day from your class spells. Select these spells from the same source as normal, such as from a spellbook for a wizard."
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "You can cast any of the spells in your collection by using a spell slot of an appropriate level. For instance, if you were level 1 and had "
                },
                {
                  "type": "ref",
                  "id": "9d83db58-4a62-5f49-b04a-55d6b4f18e7b"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": " and "
                },
                {
                  "type": "ref",
                  "id": "1c97409b-bd67-5df2-a7d3-a49aff4d3896"
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": " in your spell collection, you could cast "
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "gentle landing",
                  "marks": ["emphasis"]
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": " twice that day, "
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "force barrage",
                  "marks": ["emphasis"]
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": " twice, or each spell once."
                }
              ]
            }
          ],
          [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "Extra spell slots you gain that have additional restrictions, like the wizard's specialist school spells or the cleric's divine font spells, don't change due to this archetype, nor do such spells count toward the number of spells you place in your spell collection."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        ]
      }
    ],
    "rules": [],
    "externalIds": {
      "foundry": "Compendium.pf2e.classfeatures.Item.Upf1LXtWNJ6eB5sm"
    },
    "data": {
      "tags": ["class-archetype"]
    }
  },
  {
    "id": "3b5c4d59-a370-5cdd-a0a8-d34fcb389107",
    "pack": "secrets-of-magic",
    "kind": "class-feature",
    "slug": "class-feature:psychopomp-eidolon",
    "name": "Psychopomp Eidolon",
    "level": 1,
    "rarity": "common",
    "traits": ["summoner"],
    "sources": [
      {
        "kind": "book",
        "book": "secrets-of-magic"
      }
    ],
    "description": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Your eidolon is a psychopomp, a creature whose sworn duty is to usher souls safely to the afterlife and maintain the courts of the dead. Psychopomp eidolons have a variety of appearances, but since they often traffic with mortals, their form typically includes an elaborate mask. You and your psychopomp eidolon share an important fate together, whether it relates directly to your own soul or to a mission that will somehow protect the souls of others."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Tradition",
            "marks": ["strong"]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " divine"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Traits",
            "marks": ["strong"]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " eidolon, monitor, psychopomp"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Home Plane",
            "marks": ["strong"]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " The Boneyard"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "rule"
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Size",
            "marks": ["strong"]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " Medium"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Suggested Attacks",
            "marks": ["strong"]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " beak (piercing), claw (slashing), fist (bludgeoning), jaws (piercing), unarmed attacks shaped like a weapon"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Eidolon Attributes",
            "marks": ["strong"]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " Con +3, Int +0, Wis +1, Cha –1"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Skills",
            "marks": ["strong"]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " Intimidation, Religion"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Senses",
            "marks": ["strong"]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " darkvision"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Language",
            "marks": ["strong"]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " Requian"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Speed",
            "marks": ["strong"]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " 25 feet"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "rule"
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Initial (1st)—Spirit Touch",
            "marks": ["strong"]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " Your eidolon's attacks possess a psychopomp's ability to harm the living and the dead. Your eidolon's unarmed Strikes affect incorporeal creatures as though etched with a ghost touch property rune and deal an extra 1 void damage to living creatures and an extra 1 vitality damage to undead."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Symbiosis (7th)—Hidden Watcher",
            "marks": ["strong"]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " Your eidolon can render both of you unseen. Once per hour, they can cast invisibility as a divine innate spell targeting you, them, or both of you at once. If the spell targeted both of you, the spell ends for both of you if either of you uses a hostile action."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Transcendence (17th)—Spirit Taker",
            "marks": ["strong"]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " Your eidolon is particularly capable when it comes to handling bodiless spirits and putting undead to their final rest. Your eidolon can see incorporeal creatures inside of solid objects and can attack them with Strikes without penalty; an incorporeal creature in a solid object that takes damage from your eidolon's Strike is expelled from the object to the nearest available space, moving closer to your eidolon if possible."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Additionally, your eidolon can target or affect a creature projecting its consciousness (such as via project image) or possessing another creature, even if its body is elsewhere, though your eidolon must know about the possession or projection and choose to do so."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Finally, the spirit of an undead destroyed by your eidolon's Strikes is sent directly to the Boneyard for judgment; an undead with an ability to avoid such a fate automatically, such as a ghost's rejuvenation, can attempt a counteract check against your spell DC to return via that ability as normal. In that case, the enemy uses its Will save modifier as its counteract modifier. When your eidolon destroys an undead (even if the undead later returns), they gain temporary Hit Points equal to your level that last for 1 minute."
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "key": "Proficiency",
        "selector": "skill:intimidation",
        "rank": "trained"
      },
      {
        "key": "Proficiency",
        "selector": "skill:religion",
        "rank": "trained"
      }
    ],
    "externalIds": {
      "foundry": "Compendium.pf2e.classfeatures.Item.v7DxQ3QRa1WyTLTd"
    },
